Why don't you try it out for yourself? ;-)

NetHack has something called "wizard mode". You might check the 
Guidebook for how it is started on your system, e.g. under Dos you 
type "nethack" for starting the usual thing, and if you type 
"nethack -u wizard -D" instead, you start in Wizmode which is NetHack 
with a lot of additional features[*] and no possibility to enter the 
record file to compensate.

* - wishing for stuff, creating special monsters, level teleporting,
...

It can be used as an enhanced explore mode (you know that, don't you? 
- type 'X' while in NetHack, and say 'y'es - now you won't die but 
your score also won't show in the record). But with wizard mode you'll
also be able to experiment and find out about things, like:

What is this monster they all keep talking about?
What happens if I attack a [insert peaceful high-level monster]?
Is it possible to wish for a wand of wishing?
How many ways are there to get stoned by a cockatrice (alive or dead)?
etc.

Note: This advice is not meant as a way to discourage you from 
posting. You may ask however many questions you like (as long as they 
belong here) and most of us will gladly answer them - we'll do the 
wiztesting then. :-)
But maybe you'd like to experiment a bit for yourself...

Now for your question: 
Basically enlightenment means gaining insight/knowledge about 
something. NetHack-specific this something will be your intrinsics
(resistances, of course, but there are more like luck, alignment,
protection). Enlightenment can be used to find out whether it is safe 
to pray, and also can help in identifying rings and amulets.
A blessed potion does the same as an uncursed one but there's an 
additional benefit to it.

